{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_49","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc \"cat <<'POSE_FINAL_MESSAGE' | \\\"\"'$POSE_REVIEW_CLI\" review draft-check --draft -\ndecision: changes-requested\n\n## Review\n\nReviewed sealed bundle `rvb-8c5b48b85bb59245` (`sha256:8c5b48b85bb5924542b10d6612fd8200890d9d7c346be8acf9aca5d22872a784`). The dispatcher review-plan view returned `sha256:55a60ed8cd30be693ef9e1323b788b3e0c96d59aaff06b402bb5b1de282baaf7`. The independent review found three defects in accepted-limit identity and validation.\n\n## Criterion results\n\n| Criterion | Result | Evidence |\n|---|---|---|\n| assumption-integrity | passed | `unit:pose-mcp/go/test` |\n| backend-concurrency | passed | `integration:pose-mcp/go/writer-coordination-and-atomic-publication-integration` |\n| backend-contracts | failed (N1) | [accepted_limits.go:71](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-4264271495/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/accepted_limits.go:71) |\n| backend-input-errors | failed (N2) | [accepted_limits.go:54](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-4264271495/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/accepted_limits.go:54) |\n| backend-integration-impact | passed | `integration:pose-mcp/go/lint-spec-all-gate-contract` |\n| backend-observability | passed | `unit:pose-mcp/go/test` |\n| compatibility | failed (N1) | [accepted_limits.go:71](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-4264271495/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/accepted_limits.go:71) |\n| correctness | failed (N2) | [accepted_limits.go:54](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-4264271495/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/accepted_limits.go:54) |\n| design-causality | passed | `structure:design-79400ddcaa553202` |\n| documentation | passed | `structure:design-79400ddcaa553202` |\n| operability | failed (N2) | [accepted_limits.go:54](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-4264271495/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/accepted_limits.go:54) |\n| requirements | failed (N1, N2, N3) | [accepted_limits.go:71](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-4264271495/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/accepted_limits.go:71), [accepted_limits.go:54](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-4264271495/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/accepted_limits.go:54), [lintspec.go:1212](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-4264271495/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/cli/lintspec.go:1212) |\n| scope | passed | `structure:design-79400ddcaa553202` |\n| security | failed (N1) | [accepted_limits.go:71](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-4264271495/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/accepted_limits.go:71) |\n| solution-proportionality | passed | `structure:design-79400ddcaa553202` |\n\n## Findings\n\n- **N1 — medium, blocker:** [accepted_limits.go:71](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-4264271495/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/accepted_limits.go:71) appends limits from every spec in a roadmap or milestone without preserving the source spec or rejecting duplicate IDs. Since each spec can independently use `L1` and findings store only that ID, the brief and attestation cannot unambiguously identify which sealed limit was used.\n- **N2 — medium, blocker:** [accepted_limits.go:54](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-4264271495/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/pose/accepted_limits.go:54) accepts the phrase `Accepted because` with no explanation after it. A spec can therefore pass `lint-spec --ready-check` and seal an unjustified limit, contrary to R4.\n- **N3 — low, blocker:** [lintspec.go:1212](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-4264271495/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/cli/lintspec.go:1212) uses substring matching for ADR IDs, so an ADR containing `L10` satisfies a required reference to `L1`.\n\n## Limit judgment\n\nL1 is justified as a disclosed human-review risk for a single-spec bundle: the brief presents limit text as data, asks for a reason why a finding falls within it, and requires a dispute to be a blocking finding. L2 is justified by the plan digest and `omitempty` fields, which preserve empty-limit plan and bundle digests and make later edits require a new bundle. For one-spec reviews the gate rejects unsealed IDs and empty finding rationales. It cannot prove that a natural-language finding actually matches the limit; D1 assigns that judgment to the reviewer, so an honest independent review is part of L1'\"'s assumption. N1 is a concrete attribution flaw for composite scopes.\n\n## Validation and tool results\n\nThe focused command \"'`go -C pose-mcp test ./internal/pose ./internal/cli -run '\"'AcceptedLimit|WithinASealedLimit|ReadyCheckJudges|Brief|Conclud'\"'` passed. `surface-check` passed with one target and zero findings. Both strict `validate` invocations finished but failed because the read-only sandbox prevented Go from creating work directories and cache files; the sealed bundle contains passing `build:pose-mcp/go/build` and `unit:pose-mcp/go/test` evidence. The artifact-check command exited 0 but resolved change set `cs-6010196c7421` (head `573858...`) instead of this brief'\"'s \"'`cs-2f8efba58158`; its 19-claim/30-observation repository warnings are not treated as defects in the sealed subject. The tech-debt scan was incomplete due two invalid specs and one uncovered repository marker. The recurrence check found no flagged keys.\n\nRules applied: `.pose/workflows/review.md`, `.pose/rules/security.md`, `.pose/rules/backend-go.md` and `.pose/rules/documentation-style.md`. No relevant prior handoff was found. `review-check` and `closeout-check` remain deferred until an attestation exists; no attestation or repository edits were made.\n\n```pose-draft\n{\n  \"schema\": \"pose.review.draft/v1\",\n  \"decision\": \"changes-requested\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"N1\",\n      \"severity\": \"medium\",\n      \"disposition\": \"blocker\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/accepted_limits.go\",\n      \"line\": 71,\n      \"summary\": \"Composite roadmap or milestone plans append limits from multiple specs without preserving the source spec or checking ID collisions. Since IDs are spec-local L<N> values and findings record only limit, the brief and attestation cannot unambiguously identify which sealed limit was used; the gate accepts either one, so R3 attribution is ambiguous.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"N2\",\n      \"severity\": \"medium\",\n      \"disposition\": \"blocker\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/accepted_limits.go\",\n      \"line\": 54,\n      \"summary\": \"The ready-check treats the substring '\"'Accepted because' as a reason even when it ends the entry (for example, '- L1: assumption. Accepted because'). That unjustified limit is parsed and sealed, so R4's justification gate has a false pass.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"N3\\\",\n      \\\"severity\\\": \\\"low\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"blocker\\\",\n      \\\"file\\\": \\\"pose-mcp/internal/cli/lintspec.go\\\",\n      \\\"line\\\": 1212,\n      \\\"summary\\\": \\\"ADR coverage uses substring matching for limit IDs. An ADR mentioning L10 therefore satisfies the required reference to L1, allowing an ADR that omits L1 to pass ready-check.\\\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \\\"criteria\\\": [\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assumption-integrity\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"I examined the two sealed limits and their consumers. L1's dependence on an independent reviewer inspecting the displayed text is explicit and accepted for a single-spec review; L2 is supported by the limit's inclusion in the plan digest and optional bundle field. Semantic fit remains reviewer judgment, and N1 identifies the composite-scope ambiguity.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-concurrency\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/writer-coordination-and-atomic-publication-integration\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-contracts\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N1\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Composite review findings cannot unambiguously name one of two same-ID limits.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-input-errors\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N2\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"A limit with no text after the acceptance phrase passes validation.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-integration-impact\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/lint-spec-all-gate-contract\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"backend-observability\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"compatibility\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N1\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The new limit identity contract is ambiguous when a plan contains multiple specs.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"correctness\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N2\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The ready-check accepts an unjustified limit; N1 also affects composite reviews.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"design-causality\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-79400ddcaa553202\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"D1 addresses non-convergence by recording an explicit reviewer classification; D2 binds the limits into the plan and bundle digests. The inspected implementation follows that design, with the specific defects reported separately. The structural assessment observed no deltas.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"documentation\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-79400ddcaa553202\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"I compared the English and Portuguese manuals and their scaffold copies with runtime behavior: they describe the new section, sealed plan/bundle, review-brief/11 classification, and ready-check.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"operability\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N2\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The ready-check reports unjustified limits in normal cases but gives a false pass when the reason phrase has no explanation.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"requirements\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N1\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"R3 is ambiguous for composite scopes (N1); R4 also has false passes for empty reasons and partial ADR ID matches (N2, N3).\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"scope\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-79400ddcaa553202\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The inspected prepared subject contained the 18 implementation/documentation paths named by the spec artifacts, and the design assessment observed no structural delta.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"security\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"finding\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"N1\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"A composite-scope finding can be accepted against an ambiguous same-ID limit, weakening the integrity of the approval classification.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"solution-proportionality\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-79400ddcaa553202\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The optional sealed field, versioned brief and typed finding field are a small sufficient design for preserving review-time assumptions; the digest omission preserves existing records. The reported defects are validation gaps, not speculative architecture.\\\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \\\"tools\\\": [\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"artifact-check\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:\\\\\\\"\"'$POSE_REVIEW_CLI'\"\\\\\\\" artifact-check --spec pose-review-declared-threat-model --strict\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The command exited 0. It selected cs-6010196c7421, not the brief's cs-2f8efba58158, and reported 19 claims versus 30 observations with repository-wide orphan warnings; those warnings are not treated as scoped findings.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-design\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"structure:design-79400ddcaa553202\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Ran the recommended assessment; it observed the subject and reported no structural deltas.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-discover\\\",\n      \\\"component\\\": \\\"pose-mcp\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:\\\\\\\"\"'$POSE_REVIEW_CLI'\"\\\\\\\" assess discover --no-persist --component pose-mcp\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Ran without persistence and confirmed the pose-mcp component.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-integrate\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/review-bundle-convergence\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Ran the assessment. It reported three unobserved HTTP consumers (/admin/refresh, /healthz, /mcp), outside the changed CLI/review-limit boundary.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"assess-tech-debt\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"failed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:\\\\\\\"\"'$POSE_REVIEW_CLI'\"\\\\\\\" assess tech-debt --no-persist\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The scan was incomplete: two invalid specs were unread and one debt item was uncovered. No marker was found in the changed accepted-limit implementation.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"closeout-check\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"deferred\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The brief says closeout-check requires completion of the review; no attestation is recorded in this run.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"review-check\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"deferred\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The brief says review-check requires completion of the review; no attestation is recorded in this run.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"surface-check\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"integration:pose-mcp/go/lint-spec-all-gate-contract\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The required surface check completed with one target, 236 results and zero findings.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"validate\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"build:pose-mcp/go/build\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The required rerun could not create Go work/cache files in the read-only sandbox; the sealed bundle's pose-mcp build evidence is pass.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"validate\\\",\n      \\\"component\\\": \\\"pose-mcp\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"The required module rerun was blocked by the read-only Go work/cache paths; the sealed full pose-mcp unit result is pass, and the focused review tests also passed.\\\"\n    },\n    {\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"suggest-review\\\",\n      \\\"component\\\": \\\"pose-mcp\\\",\n      \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"passed\\\",\n      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"command:\\\\\\\"\"'$POSE_REVIEW_CLI'\"\\\\\\\" suggest review --path pose-mcp\\\",\n      \\\"rationale\\\": \\\"Ran and selected backend-go, security and documentation-style rules.\\\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n\"'```\nPOSE_FINAL_MESSAGE'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
